README.md Contents



1. Project Overview
•Description: Clear explanation of the Secure Online Notes System as an educational security project
•Purpose: Demonstrates secure coding practices for an Application Security course


2. Technology Stack
Complete table documenting:

•Frontend: Vanilla JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3
•Backend: Node.js, Express.js
•Database: PostgreSQL
•Authentication: JWT + Bcrypt
•Encryption: AES-256-CBC
•Security Middleware: Helmet.js, Express Rate Limit, CORS
•Deployment: local hosting



3. Core Features
Eight key features documented:

•User Registration & Login with secure password handling
•Role-Based Access Control (Admin/User roles)
•Secure Session Management with JWT tokens
•Password Hashing using Bcrypt (12 rounds)
•AES-256-CBC Encryption for sensitive data
•Input Validation & Sanitization
•STRIDE & DREAD Security Modeling
•Code Scanning tool integration


4. Security Implementations
Detailed explanations of security measures:

•Input Validation: validator.js for email and password validation
•Output Sanitization: Text-only treatment with DOMPurify capability
•Password Hashing: Bcrypt with 12 salt rounds
•Encryption: AES-256-CBC with per-user keys
•Session Management: JWT with 1-hour expiration
•Security Headers: Helmet.js with CSP, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options
•CORS & Rate Limiting: 100 requests per 15 minutes per IP
•Role-Based Authorization: RBAC middleware on protected routes

5. Threat Modeling Documentation

•STRIDE Threat Model: Reference to comprehensive threat analysis
•DREAD Risk Assessment: Reference to quantitative risk scoring
•Both documents linked for detailed review

